# bin/factory.d/next.crontab - the F9 ten-minute frontier timer.
# `bin/factory next --install` writes this line to the runner's crontab, replacing that target's earlier live
# line and keeping every comment and every other line; `bin/factory -C <repo> next --install` writes one more
# line that names that target (F8), with its own next-<owner>__<repo> lock and log.
# The caps match bin/overnight/driver.sh, and `flock -n` takes the next.lock the driver takes, so ticks never overlap.
# A user crontab entry runs without a login shell, so `bash -lc` loads the profile that puts
# claude, gh, and tmux on PATH. The alternative is a systemd user timer with
# OnUnitActiveSec=10min plus `loginctl enable-linger`; the merge checklist accepts either.
*/10 * * * * bash -lc 'cd ~/loam && FACTORY_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=1000000 FACTORY_GRADER_BUDGET_USD=1000000 FACTORY_MAX_PARALLEL=2 flock -n -o ~/.local/state/loam-factory/next.lock bin/factory next' >> ~/.local/state/loam-factory/next.log 2>&1
